    {
      "id": 21972,
      "name": "TheJayMann",
      "username": "TheJayMann",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-07-11T14:11:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li>It is all from 1 attack though. not multiple attacks. Even if an attack does 0 damage, it would still use it up.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Actually, if something does damage which ends up with a total of 0 (or less) then no damage is taken, thus it doesn't qualify as next damage (thus an attack of 0 will not remove stealth protection)</p>\n<p>However, irreducible damage would use up the protection, with none of the benifets of the protection.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:56:02.118Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
