      "created_at": "2013-07-11T20:12:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"TheJayMann\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/48/2261_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheJayMann:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Pydro wrote:</b><br><blockquote>4. It is all from 1 attack though. not multiple attacks. Even if an attack does 0 damage, it would still use it up.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nActually, if something does damage which ends up with a total of 0 (or less) then no damage is taken, thus it doesn't qualify as next damage (thus an attack of 0 will not remove stealth protection)However, irreducible damage would use up the protection, with none of the benifets of the protection.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That seems wrong to me. Wouldn't that make it possible for Wraith to become completely unkillable against certain villains without irreducible damage?</p>",
